Z||000003||mwbackus||05-02-2000||08:41 AM||||It is quite obvious that he had the slave pushrod out so that he could tighten the release lever.<P>Mike B.||||reg||3
Z||000004||Homicidal||05-02-2000||03:59 PM||||Then why did he say $400 one day, and nothing the next?<P>How good a mechanic can he be if he can't tell a bad cylinder from a short pushrod?<P>Besides, why did I need a longer pushrod, the other one worked just fine!||||reg||1
Z||000005||mwbackus||05-02-2000||07:09 PM||||A loose release lever will give the impression that the pushrod is too short since the lever fails to follow the pushrod correctly, and leaves a gap.  But heh, I am not trying to argue with you, I am just stating the obvious so that others may learn from your mistake.  I am sure you will be quite happy with your new clutch.<P>Mike B.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 05-02-2000).]||||reg||1
